{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"agent_message","text":"I submitted the mitigation. It's the only submission, and it was accepted as the mitigation stage.\n\n**What was wrong:** Product-catalog was failing its Postgres queries with `password authentication failed for user \"otelu\"`. Recommendation calls product-catalog, so it failed too. The Postgres log showed about 80 failed logins per minute.\n\n**What I did:** I restarted the `product-catalog` deployment with `kubectl rollout restart`. The secret `product-catalog-db-conn` and the `otelu` password were already correct, and the same connection string worked from a test pod. After the restart, failed logins dropped to zero, recommendation errors stopped, and all pods were Running with no restarts.\n\n**Caveats:**\n- I did not confirm the exact client that kept sending the bad password. The stale `otelp` credentials are only in old ReplicaSets, and no current deployment uses them. The restart cleared the failures, but I can't say for certain that the failing connection came from product-catalog.\n- Two small things I did not change: the `accounting` deployment runs a nightly image digest instead of a release tag, and the `kafka` pod uses about 550Mi of memory.\n- I did not check end-user latency through the observability stack. Only kubectl was available to me, so the submission result is the only validation I have."}}
